  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns 480. I worked it out by hand and got the same number from running it.\n\n`service2.py` imports from only two modules, `pricing` and `discounts`:\n\n1. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` = 500 + 1000 // 10 = **600**\n2. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")`: the gold discount is 20%, so 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 600 \u2212 120 = **480**\n\nNothing imports `decoy_tax.py` (which would add 25% for gold) or `decoy_shipping.py`, so they don't change the result.\n\nANSWER: 480",
